{"title":"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the area of the smallest region bounded by the graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7735059f5eff33e7d0dd6566b340906ddd0ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=|x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8b84ca3393ce6840ab42fe8edc44524e3c67e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d9e838361ca60b7c8ba39bd2c4d8af0ca3cffd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\pi\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"401\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution by e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p>The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011c4c6bfa58edca9076afb03a1f333857e6b78a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> is a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> centered at the origin. The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7735059f5eff33e7d0dd6566b340906ddd0ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=|x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> is the combined graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f08809818fd50ee3fc13182a3112bc2bd28dccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"11\" /> with a nonnegative y. Because the arguments of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f08809818fd50ee3fc13182a3112bc2bd28dccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"11\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/907ccba5e4dc9eec2ab37880d0c9538323f765a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$135^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> respectively, the angle between the graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f08809818fd50ee3fc13182a3112bc2bd28dccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"11\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, the smallest region bounded by the graphs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc031b61d006ab22dfa52ebdcd4b20b5ceaf6fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot2^2\\cdot\\pi = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME\" title=\"1979 AHSME\">1979 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1979 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 AHSME Pro